[
{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
codebase-memory-mcp is a stdio MCP server. This package installs only the
binary; it does not touch your home directory or any AI-agent configuration.

To register it with your installed AI coding agents (Claude Code, Codex CLI,
Gemini CLI, and others), run as your normal user (not root):

    codebase-memory-mcp install

This detects supported agents and edits their own config files (for example
~/.claude.json or ~/.codex/config.toml). Then restart the agent and tell it
"index this project". To wire a single agent by hand instead, add an
mcpServers entry pointing at %%PREFIX%%/bin/codebase-memory-mcp.

Indexing the FreeBSD src tree? contrib/llvm-project is the vendored LLVM
toolchain, ~27% of the tree's C/C++ files and rarely worth indexing. Copy the
sample ignore file to the src root to exclude it and cut the graph by roughly
half, while keeping FreeBSD-critical vendored code (sys/contrib/openzfs, the
device drivers under sys/contrib/dev, crypto/openssh, jemalloc) queryable:

    cp %%DOCSDIR%%/freebsd-src.cbmignore /path/to/freebsd/src/.cbmignore

The sample lists further upstreams you can add for an even smaller graph.
Editing .cbmignore only takes effect on a full re-index, not an incremental
one; ask the agent to delete and re-index the project after adding it.

EOM
}
]
